{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>וּמָחָה ה׳ אֶת שְׁמוֹ מִתַּחַת הַשָּׁמָיִם</b> — Know that the root of the souls of the people of Israel is founded in the mountains of holiness beneath the heavens, in the sod of ״הַשָּׁמַיִם כִּסְאִי״ (Isaiah 66:1), and the souls are hewn from beneath the throne of His glory, blessed be He. And understand this." "<b>And you already</b> know the sod of the name, for it is the soul, as we have elaborated in other places. And the verse says concerning the one who lords it in his heart, ״וּמָחָה ה׳ אֶת שְׁמוֹ״ — which is his soul — from its root, which is beneath the heavens. And this is the cutting off of the soul from its root." "And the verse's saying <b>וְהִבְדִּילוֹ ה׳ לְרָעָה</b> — It is difficult: after HaShem wipes out his name, what place is there for separation? Indeed, according to what has preceded us, that all the souls of the people of Israel have one root, as it says (Isaiah 60:22) ״נֵצֶר מַטָּעַי״, and as our Rabbis of blessed memory hinted (Leviticus Rabbah 4:6) on the verse ״וַיְהִי כָּל נֶפֶשׁ יֹצְאֵי יֶרֶךְ יַעֲקֹב שִׁבְעִים נָפֶשׁ״ (Exodus 1:5) — that even though they are seventy, it calls them נֶפֶשׁ (one soul), on account of the aspect of the root. Therefore, when the verse says ״וּמָחָה ה׳ אֶת שְׁמוֹ״, the verse explains that the evil portion will not be allowed to destroy the others, the man who lords it in his heart, until HaShem separates him and limits the portion that the evil reins may dominate within him, for the kelipah that holds sway is called רָעָה. And so it is the way of HaShem: when He grants permission to the destroyer, He limits for it a domain in which it may hold sway. And go forth and learn from the episode of Rava (Ta'anit 24b), when he troubled HaShem, as it were, to perform a miracle — his father had commanded him not to sleep in his place, and the destroyers held sway over his bed and not outside it — and it is for this very reason." "And the verse's saying <b>״מִכֹּל שִׁבְטֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״</b> — Because the soul is entangled with all the tribes, therefore He separates him from all of them, so that his evil will not reach another." "<b>Or</b> it may say in this manner, ״וְהִבְדִּילוֹ״ etc. — meaning that after HaShem wipes out his name, which is his soul, He will separate him unto the evil rein, to destroy him and to annihilate him with the bitter cups that are prepared for him. And this is what the verse says, ״כְּכֹל אָלוֹת״ etc. — to say that the evil that HaShem will bring upon him is an evil that encompasses all the curses which he had schemed to escape."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:15.387587690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}